{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  SehatUP article template - redesign
  ============================================================================
  Replaces sections/main-article.liquid. Keep the old file as main-article.bak
  so a bad deploy is one rename away from a rollback.

  WHAT THIS SECTION OWNS
    hero, title, article body typography, the formulation panel, the
    consultation rail, the Latest blogs list, the back link.

  ONE CARD, ONE TITLE
    The article is a bordered card. The featured image sits flush inside the
    top of it, the <h1> sits directly under the image, then the byline row.
    Nothing is duplicated and there is no separate hero band: the banner is the
    picture, the h1 is the title, read in that order. The image is always full
    card width at its own aspect ratio, which is what caps its height - a 16:9
    banner in a 920px column is 517px tall whatever the viewport does.

  WHY SO LITTLE COPY IS IN THE SETTINGS
    Section settings belong to the template, so anything typed there shows on
    every post in the blog. Per-post content comes from the article itself or
    from a metafield:
      article.metafields.custom.faqs       the FAQ (written in the body, see below)
      article.metafields.custom.formulation the ingredient panel, JSON
      article.metafields.custom.reviewed_by the byline reviewer, single line text

  WHAT IT DEPENDS ON
    snippets/sehatup-attribution     for utm capture (optional, degrades fine)
    blog-lead-sheet.gs               the Apps Script that writes the sheet row

  THE FAQ IS NOT OURS
    The FAQs live inside article.content as <div class="faq-section"> with
    native <details>, written by hand in the Shopify editor. This section
    renders no FAQ of its own and emits no FAQPage JSON-LD. It only styles
    what is already there.

  INSTALL
    1. Themes -> Edit code -> Sections -> main-article.liquid
       Copy the current contents into a new file main-article-old.liquid first.
    2. Paste this file over main-article.liquid.
    3. Customize -> Blog posts -> if the standalone "FAQ accordion" section is
       still on the article template, remove it. article.metafields.custom.faqs
       is empty on these posts, so it falls through to its preset placeholder
       blocks and prints three FAQs nobody wrote.
    4. Set up the sheet: follow the INSTALL block in blog-lead-sheet.gs, then
       paste the Apps Script /exec URL into "Lead endpoint URL" and the same
       token into "Shared token". Until the URL is set the form validates and
       shows its success state but posts nothing, and logs a console warning
       saying so.

  DESIGN NOTES
    Red is reserved for actions. Nothing decorative is red, so the one red
    button on screen is always the thing to press. Wine carries structure and
    the formulation panel. Green appears only on affirmative list markers.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign words = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
  assign read_min = words | divided_by: 220 | plus: 1

  assign byline = section.settings.byline
  if byline == blank
    assign byline = article.author
  endif

  # Formulation panel. Per post via metafield; the section blocks are only a
  # fallback, and are off by default so a men's formula never lands on a
  # women's post.
  assign fm = article.metafields.custom.formulation.value
  assign herbs = fm.herbs
  if herbs == blank
    assign herbs = fm
  endif
  assign panel_from = ''
  if herbs.size > 0
    assign panel_from = 'metafield'
  elsif section.settings.panel_fallback and section.blocks.size > 0
    assign panel_from = 'blocks'
  endif
-%}

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link
  rel="stylesheet"
  href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400;1,600&display=swap"
>

<div
  class="su-post"
  id="su-post-{{ section.id }}"
  data-su-post
  data-endpoint="{{ section.settings.lead_endpoint | escape }}"
  data-collection="{{ section.settings.lead_collection | default: 'Blog leads' }}"
  data-token="{{ section.settings.lead_token | escape }}"
  data-article-handle="{{ article.handle }}"
  data-article-title="{{ article.title | escape }}"
  data-bar-at="{{ section.settings.bar_trigger | default: 22 }}"
  data-show-bar="{{ section.settings.show_mobile_bar }}"
  data-progress="{{ section.settings.show_progress }}"
  style="
    --su-brand: {{ section.settings.color_brand }};
    --su-brand-deep: {{ section.settings.color_brand_deep }};
    --su-wine: {{ section.settings.color_wine }};
    --su-sticky-top: {{ section.settings.sticky_top | default: 20 }}px;
  "
>
  {%- if section.settings.show_progress -%}
    <div class="su-progress" aria-hidden="true"><i data-su-progress-fill></i></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------------- article {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="su-shell">
    <article class="su-card">
      {%- if article.image -%}
        <figure
          class="su-card__art su-card__art--{{ section.settings.banner_fit | default: 'fit' }}"
          style="
            --su-banner-ratio: {{ article.image.aspect_ratio }};
            --su-banner-h: {{ section.settings.banner_height | default: 320 }}px;
            --su-banner-y: {{ section.settings.banner_focus | default: 0 }}%;
          "
        >
          <img
            src="{{ article.image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
            srcset="
              {% if article.image.width >= 600 %}{{ article.image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,{% endif %}
              {% if article.image.width >= 900 %}{{ article.image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,{% endif %}
              {% if article.image.width >= 1200 %}{{ article.image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w,{% endif %}
              {% if article.image.width >= 1600 %}{{ article.image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w{% endif %}
            "
            sizes="(min-width: 990px) 920px, calc(100vw - 40px)"
            width="{{ article.image.width }}"
            height="{{ article.image.height }}"
            alt="{{ article.image.alt | escape }}"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          >
        </figure>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="su-card__body su-main">
        <header class="su-card__head">
          <h1 class="su-card__title">{{ article.title | escape }}</h1>
          <p class="su-meta">
            <time datetime="{{ article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">
              {{- article.published_at | date: '%d %B %Y' -}}
            </time>
            <span class="su-meta__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>{{ read_min }} min read</span>
            {%- if byline != blank -%}
              <span class="su-meta__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span>By {{ byline | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if reviewer != blank -%}
              <span class="su-meta__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="su-meta__review">Reviewed by {{ reviewer | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="su-rte su-rte--lead" data-su-rte>
          {{ article.content }}
        </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---------------------------- signature: formulation panel {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if panel_from != blank -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign p_title = fm.title | default: section.settings.panel_title
          assign p_note  = fm.note  | default: section.settings.panel_note
          assign p_url   = fm.url   | default: section.settings.panel_link
        -%}
        <aside class="su-formula" data-su-formula aria-labelledby="su-formula-{{ section.id }}">
          <div class="su-formula__head">
            <p class="su-eyebrow su-formula__kicker">{{ section.settings.panel_kicker | escape }}</p>
            <h2 class="su-formula__title" id="su-formula-{{ section.id }}">{{ p_title | escape }}</h2>
          </div>

          <ul class="su-formula__list">
            {%- if panel_from == 'metafield' -%}
              {%- for h in herbs -%}
                <li class="su-herb">
                  <div class="su-herb__id">
                    <span class="su-herb__name">{{ h.name | escape }}</span>
                    {%- if h.botanical != blank -%}
                      <span class="su-herb__botanical">{{ h.botanical | escape }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                  {%- if h.use != blank -%}
                    <p class="su-herb__use">{{ h.use | escape }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                <li class="su-herb" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <div class="su-herb__id">
                    <span class="su-herb__name">{{ block.settings.name | escape }}</span>
                    {%- if block.settings.botanical != blank -%}
                      <span class="su-herb__botanical">{{ block.settings.botanical | escape }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                  {%- if block.settings.use != blank -%}
                    <p class="su-herb__use">{{ block.settings.use | escape }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>

          <div class="su-formula__foot">
            {%- if p_note != blank -%}
              <p class="su-formula__note">{{ p_note | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if p_url != blank -%}
              <a class="su-formula__cta" href="{{ p_url }}">
                {{ section.settings.panel_link_label | escape }}
                <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M3 8h9M8.5 4.5 12 8l-3.5 3.5"/></svg>
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </aside>
      {%- endif -%}

        <p class="su-back">
        <a href="{{ blog.url }}">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M13 8H4M7.5 4.5 4 8l3.5 3.5"/></svg>
          All {{ blog.title | downcase | escape }}
        </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    {%- comment -%} --------------------------------------------------- rail {%- endcomment -%}
    <aside class="su-rail" data-su-rail>
      {%- if section.settings.show_cta -%}
        <div class="su-rail__stick">
        <div class="su-consult" data-su-consult>
          <div class="su-consult__body" data-su-consult-body>
            {%- if section.settings.cta_status != blank -%}
              <p class="su-consult__status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ section.settings.cta_status | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="su-consult__title">{{ section.settings.cta_title | escape }}</h2>
            <p class="su-consult__dek">{{ section.settings.cta_dek | escape }}</p>

            <form class="su-form" data-su-form novalidate>
              <div class="su-field">
                <label class="su-label" for="su-name-{{ section.id }}">Your name</label>
                <input
                  class="su-input"
                  id="su-name-{{ section.id }}"
                  name="name"
                  type="text"
                  autocomplete="name"
                  maxlength="60"
                  placeholder="Full name"
                  aria-describedby="su-name-err-{{ section.id }}"
                  required
                >
                <p class="su-err" id="su-name-err-{{ section.id }}" data-su-err="name"></p>
              </div>

              <div class="su-field">
                <label class="su-label" for="su-phone-{{ section.id }}">Mobile number</label>
                <div class="su-phone">
                  <span class="su-phone__cc" aria-hidden="true">+91</span>
                  <input
                    class="su-input su-input--phone"
                    id="su-phone-{{ section.id }}"
                    name="phone"
                    type="tel"
                    inputmode="numeric"
                    autocomplete="tel-national"
                    placeholder="10 digit number"
                    aria-describedby="su-phone-err-{{ section.id }}"
                    required
                  >
                </div>
                <p class="su-err" id="su-phone-err-{{ section.id }}" data-su-err="phone"></p>
              </div>

              {%- if section.settings.show_topic -%}
                <div class="su-field">
                  <label class="su-label" for="su-topic-{{ section.id }}">What should the doctor know?</label>
                  <select class="su-input su-select" id="su-topic-{{ section.id }}" name="topic">
                    <option value="">Pick one</option>
                    {%- assign topics = section.settings.topics | split: ',' -%}
                    {%- for t in topics -%}
                      <option value="{{ t | strip | escape }}">{{ t | strip | escape }}</option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              <div class="su-hp" aria-hidden="true">
                <label for="su-city-{{ section.id }}">City</label>
                <input id="su-city-{{ section.id }}" name="city_confirm" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
              </div>

              <button class="su-btn" type="submit" data-su-submit>
                <span data-su-btn-label>{{ section.settings.cta_button | escape }}</span>
                <i class="su-spin" aria-hidden="true"></i>
              </button>

              <p class="su-consent">
                {{ section.settings.cta_consent | escape }}
                {%- if section.settings.privacy_url != blank %}
                  <a href="{{ section.settings.privacy_url }}">Privacy policy</a>.
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>
            </form>
          </div>

          <div class="su-done" data-su-done hidden>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m4 12.5 5 5L20 7"/></svg>
            <h2 class="su-done__title">{{ section.settings.done_title | escape }}</h2>
            <p class="su-done__dek">{{ section.settings.done_dek | escape }}</p>
          </div>

          <p class="su-live" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-su-live></p>

          <div class="su-consult__foot">
          <ul class="su-trust">
            {%- if section.settings.trust_1 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.trust_1 | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.trust_2 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.trust_2 | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.trust_3 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.trust_3 | escape }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          </ul>

          {%- if section.settings.whatsapp_url != blank -%}
            <a class="su-wa" href="{{ section.settings.whatsapp_url }}" rel="noopener">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="15" height="15" aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 0a8 8 0 0 0-6.8 12.2L0 16l3.9-1.2A8 8 0 1 0 8 0Zm4.6 11.3c-.2.5-1.1 1-1.5 1-.4.1-.9.1-1.4-.1a12 12 0 0 1-4.6-4c-.3-.5-.6-1.2-.6-1.8 0-.7.4-1.1.6-1.3a.7.7 0 0 1 .5-.2h.4c.1 0 .3 0 .5.4l.6 1.4c0 .1.1.3 0 .4l-.3.4-.2.3c-.1.1-.2.2 0 .4a8 8 0 0 0 3.2 2.5c.2.1.3.1.4 0l.7-.9c.1-.2.2-.1.4-.1l1.4.7c.2.1.3.2.4.3v.6Z"/></svg>
            {{ section.settings.whatsapp_label | escape }}
          </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------ latest blogs {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
      {%- assign limit = section.settings.latest_count | default: 4 -%}
      {%- if blog.articles.size > 1 -%}
        <nav class="su-latest" aria-labelledby="su-latest-{{ section.id }}">
          <p class="su-latest__label" id="su-latest-{{ section.id }}">
            {{ section.settings.latest_title | escape }}
          </p>

          <ul class="su-latest__list">
            {%- for a in blog.articles -%}
              {%- if a.id == article.id -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if shown >= limit -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign a_words = a.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size -%}
              {%- assign a_min = a_words | divided_by: 220 | plus: 1 -%}
              <li class="su-latest__item">
                <a href="{{ a.url }}">
                  {%- if a.image -%}
                    <span class="su-latest__thumb">
                      <img
                        src="{{ a.image | image_url: width: 200 }}"
                        srcset="{{ a.image | image_url: width: 200 }} 200w, {{ a.image | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w"
                        sizes="88px"
                        width="{{ a.image.width }}"
                        height="{{ a.image.height }}"
                        alt=""
                        loading="lazy"
                      >
                    </span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      No featured image. A tinted tile with the first letter beats a
                      broken box and beats a gap, and it keeps every row the same
                      height so the list still scans as a column.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span class="su-latest__thumb su-latest__thumb--empty" aria-hidden="true">
                      {{- a.title | strip | truncate: 1, '' | upcase -}}
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  <span class="su-latest__text">
                    <span class="su-latest__title">{{ a.title | escape }}</span>
                    <span class="su-latest__meta">
                      {{ a.published_at | date: '%d %b %Y' }}
                      <span class="su-latest__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      {{ a_min }} min read
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>

          <a class="su-latest__all" href="{{ blog.url }}">
            All {{ blog.title | downcase | escape }}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M3 8h9M8.5 4.5 12 8l-3.5 3.5"/></svg>
          </a>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}
    </aside>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} -------------------------------------------- mobile cta bar {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_cta and section.settings.show_mobile_bar -%}
    <div class="su-bar" data-su-bar hidden>
      <p class="su-bar__text">{{ section.settings.bar_text | escape }}</p>
      <button class="su-bar__btn" type="button" data-su-bar-btn>
        {{ section.settings.bar_button | escape }}
      </button>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
.su-post {
  /* Neutral, not warm. The old ink and body carried violet, the lines and
     surfaces carried pink, and together with wine headings the whole page read
     purple even where nothing was purple. Wine survives only as a surface. */
  --su-ink: #111111;
  --su-body: #3a3a3a;
  --su-muted: #6e6e6e;
  --su-wine: #55123a;
  --su-wine-2: #7a1a4b;
  --su-brand: #ee204a;
  --su-brand-deep: #c8143a;
  --su-brand-tint: rgba(238, 32, 74, 0.09);
  --su-leaf: #2f6b4f;
  --su-paper: #ffffff;
  --su-surface: #f7f7f8;
  --su-line: #e6e6e6;
  --su-sticky-top: 20px;

  /* One family. Hierarchy is carried by weight, size and tracking rather
     than by a second face, so headings run heavier and tighter than they
     would if a display serif were doing that work. */
  --su-display: Inter, sans-serif;
  --su-sans: Inter, sans-serif;

  background: var(--su-paper);
  color: var(--su-body);
  font-family: var(--su-sans);
  font-size: 17.5px;
  line-height: 1.72;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

.su-post *:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--su-brand);
  outline-offset: 2px;
  border-radius: 3px;
}

.su-eyebrow {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- progress */
.su-progress {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0 0 auto 0;
  height: 2px;
  z-index: 40;
  background: transparent;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.su-progress i {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  width: 0;
  background: var(--su-brand);
  transition: width 90ms linear;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- article card
   The article is an object on the page now, not a column of text bleeding into
   the background. The banner sits flush inside the top of the card, the title
   sits directly under it, and the byline follows. Nothing is duplicated: the
   banner is picture, the h1 is the title, and they are read in that order.

   The image is full card width at its own aspect ratio. That is what fixed the
   height problem for good - a 16:9 banner in a 920px column is 517px tall
   whatever the viewport does, so there is nothing left to cap. */
.su-card {
  min-width: 0;
  background: var(--su-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
/* The banner is capped in height, and the whole picture is kept.

   Height cannot come down without either cropping or leaving space at the
   sides. Cropping lost the bottom of the artwork, so the space wins: the
   picture is mounted on a tinted panel and sits whole inside it, the way a
   photograph sits on a board. The panel is a deliberate surface rather than
   an accidental gap, which is the difference between framing and letterboxing.

   Fill mode is there for banners drawn to bleed. It crops from the top down,
   because that is where these banners put their title.

   width:100% is not optional in either mode. With width auto, a max-height
   that bites makes the height definite and the browser derives the width back
   from the ratio, so the frame shrinks sideways instead. */
.su-card__art {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: var(--su-banner-ratio, 1.78);
  max-height: var(--su-banner-h, 320px);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.su-card__art--fit {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: clamp(14px, 2.2vw, 24px);
  background: var(--su-surface);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--su-line);
}
.su-card__art--fit img {
  display: block;
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  max-width: 100%;
  max-height: 100%;
  border-radius: 8px;
}

.su-card__art--fill {
  background: var(--su-surface);
}
.su-card__art--fill img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: 50% var(--su-banner-y, 0%);
}

.su-card__body { padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 40px); }

.su-card__head {
  padding-bottom: 22px;
  margin-bottom: 26px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--su-line);
}
.su-card__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 36px);
  line-height: 1.16;
  letter-spacing: -0.032em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.su-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 9px;
  margin: 14px 0 0;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--su-muted);
}
.su-meta__dot {
  width: 3px;
  height: 3px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: #c9c9c9;
}
.su-meta__review { color: var(--su-leaf); font-weight: 600; }

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- shell */
.su-shell {
  max-width: 1320px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 34px) clamp(16px, 4vw, 32px) 72px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 24px;
}
.su-main { min-width: 0; }

/* ------------------------------------------------------- article body
   Descendant selectors, not child selectors: the FAQ ships inside
   article.content wrapped in a .faq-section div, so anything scoped to
   direct children would skip it entirely.

   Every rule is prefixed with .su-post so it outranks the inline <style>
   that travels with that FAQ markup. At equal specificity that <style>
   would win on source order, because it sits in the body and this sits in
   the head.

   Nothing of ours is ever nested inside .su-rte. The consultation card and
   the formulation panel are placed BETWEEN two .su-rte containers, which is
   what the split in the script below is for. */
.su-post .su-rte { max-width: 72ch; }
.su-post .su-rte > *:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
.su-post .su-rte--tail { margin-top: 52px; }

.su-post .su-rte p { margin: 0 0 20px; }
.su-post .su-rte--lead > p:first-of-type {
  font-size: 19px;
  line-height: 1.62;
  color: var(--su-ink);
}

.su-post .su-rte h2 {
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: clamp(23px, 2.3vw, 29px);
  line-height: 1.22;
  letter-spacing: -0.024em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  margin: 0 0 18px;
  padding-top: 26px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.su-post .su-rte h2:not(:first-child) { margin-top: 52px; }

.su-post .su-rte h3 {
  font-family: var(--su-sans);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 18px;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  margin: 34px 0 10px;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
}
.su-post .su-rte h4 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--su-ink); margin: 26px 0 8px; }

.su-post .su-rte ul,
.su-post .su-rte ol { margin: 0 0 22px; padding-left: 0; list-style: none; }
.su-post .su-rte ul > li,
.su-post .su-rte ol > li { position: relative; padding-left: 26px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.su-post .su-rte ul > li::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 6px;
  top: 0.72em;
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--su-brand);
}
.su-post .su-rte ol { counter-reset: su-ol; }
.su-post .su-rte ol > li { counter-increment: su-ol; }
.su-post .su-rte ol > li::before {
  content: counter(su-ol);
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0.1em;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.su-post .su-rte a {
  color: var(--su-brand);
  font-weight: 500;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  transition: border-color 140ms ease;
}
.su-post .su-rte a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--su-brand); }
.su-post .su-rte strong { color: var(--su-ink); font-weight: 700; }
.su-post .su-rte em { font-style: italic; }
/* A <strong> inside a link declares its own colour, which beats the brand
   colour the link would otherwise pass down by inheritance. Re-assert it. */
.su-post .su-rte a strong,
.su-post .su-rte a em,
.su-post .su-rte strong a { color: var(--su-brand); }
.su-post .su-rte img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; }
.su-post .su-rte blockquote {
  margin: 28px 0;
  padding: 4px 0 4px 22px;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--su-brand);
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 19px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
}

/* ------------------------------ FAQ, written by hand in article.content
   Matches any <details> in the body, so a post that skips the
   .faq-section wrapper still gets the accordion. */
.su-post .su-rte .faq-section { width: auto; margin: 52px 0 0; }
.su-post .su-rte .faq-section h2 { margin-bottom: 4px; }

.su-post .su-rte details {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--su-line);
}
.su-post .su-rte summary {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 16px;
  min-height: 56px;
  padding: 14px 4px;
  list-style: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-family: var(--su-sans);
  font-size: 16.5px;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  transition: color 130ms ease;
}
.su-post .su-rte summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.su-post .su-rte summary:hover { color: var(--su-brand); }
.su-post .su-rte summary::after {
  content: "";
  flex: none;
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  margin: -4px 8px 0 0;
  border-right: 1.7px solid var(--su-muted);
  border-bottom: 1.7px solid var(--su-muted);
  transform: rotate(45deg);
  transition: transform 200ms ease;
}
.su-post .su-rte details[open] summary::after { margin-top: 4px; transform: rotate(-135deg); }
.su-post .su-rte details p {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 4px 20px;
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.7;
  color: var(--su-body);
}
.su-post .su-rte details[open] > *:not(summary) { animation: su-reveal 220ms ease both; }
@keyframes su-reveal {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-4px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}

/* -------------------------------------------- signature: formulation */
.su-formula {
  margin: 56px 0 0;
  max-width: 72ch;
  border-radius: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86);
  background: linear-gradient(155deg, var(--su-wine) 0%, #380b26 100%);
}
.su-formula__head {
  padding: 26px 28px 20px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
}
.su-formula__kicker { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); }
.su-formula__title {
  margin: 10px 0 0;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 25px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  color: #fff;
}
.su-formula__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.su-herb {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 4px;
  padding: 18px 28px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}
.su-herb__name {
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 18px;
  letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  line-height: 1.3;
  color: #fff;
}
.su-herb__botanical {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 3px;
  font-size: 10.5px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.48);
}
.su-herb__use { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
.su-formula__foot {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 14px;
  padding: 20px 28px 24px;
}
.su-formula__note {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
}
.su-formula__cta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 7px;
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #fff;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  padding-bottom: 2px;
}
.su-formula__cta:hover { border-bottom-color: #fff; }

.su-back { margin: 44px 0 0; }
.su-back a {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.su-back a:hover { color: var(--su-brand); }

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------- rail */
.su-rail { min-width: 0; }
/* The rail stretches to the full grid row on purpose. align-self:start would
   collapse it to its content height and the sticky card would scroll away
   halfway down the article, which is the one thing it must not do. */

/* ------------------------------------------------------- consultation
   No accent stripe. The card is split into two zones instead: a white ask,
   and a tinted band underneath that answers the question the ask provokes.
   Structure does the work a decorative edge was doing, and the red button
   stays the only loud thing on the page.

   Figure and ground are inverted from the first pass too. The card is white
   and the fields carry the tint, so the thing you type into is the recessed
   thing rather than the raised one. */
.su-consult {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  border-radius: 16px;
  background: var(--su-paper);
  box-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(26, 18, 32, 0.05),
    0 14px 30px -16px rgba(26, 18, 32, 0.22);
}
.su-consult__body { padding: 20px 18px 18px; }

.su-consult__status {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  margin: 0 0 10px;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  color: var(--su-leaf);
}
.su-consult__status span {
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--su-leaf);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(47, 107, 79, 0.16);
}

.su-consult__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 19px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
}
.su-consult__dek {
  margin: 6px 0 16px;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--su-muted);
}

.su-field { margin-bottom: 11px; }
.su-label {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.002em;
  color: var(--su-muted);
}
.su-input {
  width: 100%;
  height: 48px;
  padding: 0 13px;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  background: var(--su-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  border-radius: 9px;
  transition: border-color 130ms ease, box-shadow 130ms ease, background 130ms ease;
}
.su-input::placeholder { color: #a79fad; font-weight: 400; }
.su-input:focus {
  outline: none;
  background: var(--su-paper);
  border-color: var(--su-brand);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--su-brand-tint);
}
.su-select { appearance: none; padding-right: 34px; cursor: pointer; }
.su-phone { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; }
.su-phone__cc {
  position: absolute;
  left: 13px;
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--su-muted);
  pointer-events: none;
}
.su-input--phone { padding-left: 47px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }

.su-err { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--su-brand-deep); display: none; }
.su-field.is-bad .su-input { border-color: var(--su-brand-deep); background: var(--su-paper); }
.su-field.is-bad .su-err { display: block; }

.su-hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }

.su-btn {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 50px;
  margin-top: 6px;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 9px;
  background: var(--su-brand);
  color: #fff;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 15.5px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 140ms ease, transform 140ms ease, box-shadow 140ms ease;
  box-shadow: 0 6px 14px -8px rgba(238, 32, 74, 0.7);
}
.su-btn:hover { background: var(--su-brand-deep); box-shadow: 0 8px 18px -8px rgba(200, 20, 58, 0.75); }
.su-btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); box-shadow: none; }
.su-btn[disabled] { opacity: 0.72; cursor: default; box-shadow: none; }
.su-spin {
  display: none;
  width: 14px;
  height: 14px;
  margin-left: 9px;
  vertical-align: -2px;
  border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  border-top-color: #fff;
  border-radius: 50%;
  animation: su-spin 620ms linear infinite;
}
.su-form.is-busy .su-spin { display: inline-block; }
@keyframes su-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }

.su-consent { margin: 11px 0 0; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--su-muted); }
.su-consent a { color: var(--su-muted); text-decoration: underline; }

.su-done { text-align: center; padding: 34px 22px 30px; color: var(--su-leaf); }
.su-done__title {
  margin: 12px 0 0;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 20px;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
}
.su-done__dek { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--su-muted); }

.su-live { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }

/* The reassurance band. Same tint as the fields, so the card reads as one
   material with two jobs rather than two stacked cards. */
.su-consult__foot {
  padding: 12px 14px 13px;
  background: var(--su-surface);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--su-line);
}
/* One line, three claims.

   Three separate markers cost 42px of indent and made the row wrap. One tick
   at the head now covers all three - they are a single guarantee, not three
   badges - and thin dots separate them. That is what buys the line, more than
   the smaller type does.

   nowrap is deliberate: these labels are settings, and if someone types a long
   one the row should truncate visibly rather than quietly go back to two lines. */
.su-trust {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0;
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 0 0 15px;
  position: relative;
  min-width: 0;
}
.su-trust::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 50%;
  width: 8px;
  height: 4px;
  margin-top: -3px;
  border-left: 1.6px solid var(--su-leaf);
  border-bottom: 1.6px solid var(--su-leaf);
  transform: rotate(-45deg);
}
.su-trust li {
  flex: 0 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.002em;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--su-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
.su-trust li + li::before {
  content: "";
  display: inline-block;
  width: 2px;
  height: 2px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  margin: 0 6px;
  vertical-align: 2px;
  background: currentColor;
  opacity: 0.5;
}

.su-wa {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 7px;
  margin-top: 11px;
  padding-top: 11px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  width: 100%;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  color: var(--su-leaf);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.su-wa:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

/* -------------------------------------------------------- latest blogs
   A thumbnail, a two-line title, then the date and read time. The clamp is
   what makes the list scan: every row is the same height whether the headline
   is four words or fourteen, so the eye runs down the thumbnails instead of a
   ragged left edge. */
.su-latest {
  margin-top: 20px;
  background: var(--su-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  border-radius: 16px;
  padding: 18px 18px 16px;
}
.su-latest__label {
  margin: 0 0 4px;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--su-ink);
}
.su-latest__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.su-latest__item { border-top: 1px solid var(--su-line); }
.su-latest__item a {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 12px;
  padding: 14px 0;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.su-latest__thumb {
  flex: none;
  width: 76px;
  height: 58px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--su-surface);
}
.su-latest__thumb img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
}
.su-latest__thumb--empty {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #b9b9bd;
}

.su-latest__text { min-width: 0; }
.su-latest__title {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
  font-family: var(--su-display);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.35;
  letter-spacing: -0.014em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  transition: color 130ms ease;
}
.su-latest__item a:hover .su-latest__title { color: var(--su-brand); }
.su-latest__meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  margin-top: 5px;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--su-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.su-latest__dot {
  width: 2px;
  height: 2px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: currentColor;
  opacity: 0.6;
}

.su-latest__all {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 7px;
  width: 100%;
  margin-top: 6px;
  padding-top: 14px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--su-line);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  color: var(--su-ink);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.su-latest__all:hover { color: var(--su-brand); }

/* ------------------------------------------------------------ mobile bar */
.su-bar {
  position: fixed;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  z-index: 30;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 14px;
  padding: 11px 84px 11px 18px;
  padding-bottom: calc(11px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
  background: var(--su-wine);
  transform: translateY(100%);
  transition: transform 240ms ease;
}
.su-bar.is-up { transform: translateY(0); }
.su-bar__text {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1.3;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
}
.su-bar__btn {
  flex: none;
  min-height: 42px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 9px;
  background: var(--su-brand);
  color: #fff;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 700;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.su-bar__btn:hover { background: var(--su-brand-deep); }

/* --------------------------------------------------------- breakpoints */
@media (min-width: 750px) {
  .su-herb { grid-template-columns: 190px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; align-items: baseline; }
}

@media (min-width: 990px) {
  .su-shell { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px; gap: 24px; }
  /* Flex column so the Latest list can sit at the foot of the rail: the CTA
     travels with the reader, the list waits at the finish line. */
  .su-rail { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  /* The sticky card lives in a growing box, so it stops travelling exactly
     where the Latest list begins instead of sliding over it. */
  .su-rail__stick { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
  .su-latest { flex: none; }
  .su-consult { position: sticky; top: var(--su-sticky-top); }
  .su-bar { display: none; }
}

@media (min-width: 1200px) {
  .su-shell { gap: 28px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 308px; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .su-post *,
  .su-post *::before,
  .su-post *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
(function () {
  'use strict';

  var roots = document.querySelectorAll('[data-su-post]');
  if (!roots.length) return;

  Array.prototype.forEach.call(roots, function (root) {
    if (root.dataset.suReady) return;
    root.dataset.suReady = '1';

    var form = root.querySelector('[data-su-form]');
    var consult = root.querySelector('[data-su-consult]');
    var body = root.querySelector('[data-su-consult-body]');
    var done = root.querySelector('[data-su-done]');
    var live = root.querySelector('[data-su-live]');
    var bar = root.querySelector('[data-su-bar]');
    var fill = root.querySelector('[data-su-progress-fill]');
    var rte = root.querySelector('[data-su-rte]');
    /* Progress and the mobile bar measure the whole column, not just the
       first chunk of body copy: the split below shortens [data-su-rte]. */
    var track = root.querySelector('.su-card') || rte;
    var rail = root.querySelector('[data-su-rail]');
    var handle = root.dataset.articleHandle || '';
    var doneKey = 'su_lead_' + handle;

    /* ---------------------------------------------------- sticky offset

       The offset exists for one reason: to clear a header that stays on screen.
       A header that scrolls away needs no clearance, so measuring its height
       unconditionally was wrong - it left a 96px default in place, and because
       a sticky element clamps to its top offset even at scroll 0, the CTA
       started 62px below the top of the article card and the two columns did
       not line up. Position, then height. */
    function measureHeader() {
      var header = document.querySelector('.section-header, header.header-wrapper, #shopify-section-header, body > header');
      var pinned = false;
      var h = 0;
      if (header) {
        var pos = window.getComputedStyle(header).position;
        pinned = pos === 'fixed' || pos === 'sticky';
        h = header.getBoundingClientRect().height;
      }
      var top = (pinned && h > 0 && h < 220) ? Math.round(h + 20) : 20;
      root.style.setProperty('--su-sticky-top', top + 'px');
    }
    measureHeader();
    window.addEventListener('resize', measureHeader, { passive: true });

    /* ------------------------------------------------------ progress bar */
    if (fill) {
      var tick = function () {
        var box = track ? track.getBoundingClientRect() : null;
        if (!box) return;
        var total = box.height - window.innerHeight;
        var seen = -box.top;
        var pct = total > 0 ? Math.min(1, Math.max(0, seen / total)) : 0;
        fill.style.width = (pct * 100).toFixed(2) + '%';
      };
      window.addEventListener('scroll', tick, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', tick, { passive: true });
      tick();
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------ placing things mid-article
       The article body is one blob of merchant HTML, and the FAQ lives
       inside it. We never nest our own components in .su-rte, because the
       body type rules would repaint them. Instead we cut the blob and drop
       the component into the seam. */
    function splitFrom(host, anchor) {
      var tail = document.createElement('div');
      tail.className = 'su-rte su-rte--tail';
      var node = anchor;
      while (node) {
        var next = node.nextSibling;
        tail.appendChild(node);
        node = next;
      }
      host.parentNode.insertBefore(tail, host.nextSibling);
      return tail;
    }

    function directChildren(host, sel) {
      return Array.prototype.filter.call(host.children, function (el) {
        return el.matches(sel);
      });
    }

    /* The formulation panel belongs with the herbs, not after the FAQ.
       Cut at the FAQ and slot the panel into the gap. */
    var formula = root.querySelector('[data-su-formula]');
    if (formula && rte) {
      var faqAt = directChildren(rte, '.faq-section')[0];
      if (!faqAt) {
        faqAt = directChildren(rte, 'h2').filter(function (h) {
          return /frequently asked|^faqs?\b/i.test(h.textContent.trim());
        })[0];
      }
      if (faqAt) {
        var faqTail = splitFrom(rte, faqAt);
        rte.parentNode.insertBefore(formula, faqTail);
      }
    }

    /* The card is NOT moved into the article on mobile.

       In one column the rail already follows the article, so the consultation
       card lands at the end on its own - which is where it belongs. Injecting
       a form into the middle of someone's reading interrupts it, and the
       sticky bar below is the thing that keeps the offer available until they
       get there. The bar hides itself once the card is actually on screen, so
       the two never ask at the same time. */

    /* ------------------------------------------------------- mobile bar */
    if (bar && consult) {
      var barBtn = root.querySelector('[data-su-bar-btn]');
      var at = parseInt(root.dataset.barAt || '22', 10) / 100;

      var toggleBar = function () {
        if (sessionStorage.getItem(doneKey)) { bar.classList.remove('is-up'); return; }
        var box = track ? track.getBoundingClientRect() : null;
        if (!box) return;
        var passed = -box.top > box.height * at;
        var cardBox = consult.getBoundingClientRect();
        var cardVisible = cardBox.top < window.innerHeight - 80 && cardBox.bottom > 80;
        if (passed && !cardVisible) {
          bar.hidden = false;
          bar.classList.add('is-up');
        } else {
          bar.classList.remove('is-up');
        }
      };
      window.addEventListener('scroll', toggleBar, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', toggleBar, { passive: true });
      toggleBar();

      if (barBtn) {
        barBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
          consult.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
          var first = consult.querySelector('input[name="name"]');
          if (first) window.setTimeout(function () { first.focus({ preventScroll: true }); }, 420);
        });
      }
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- form */
    if (!form) return;

    /* Already submitted this visit: show the receipt, not the ask. */
    try {
      if (sessionStorage.getItem(doneKey)) showDone();
    } catch (e) { /* private mode */ }

    var nameEl = form.querySelector('input[name="name"]');
    var phoneEl = form.querySelector('input[name="phone"]');
    var topicEl = form.querySelector('[name="topic"]');
    var hpEl = form.querySelector('input[name="city_confirm"]');
    var btn = form.querySelector('[data-su-submit]');
    var btnLabel = form.querySelector('[data-su-btn-label]');
    var sending = false;

    /* Normalise as they type, so every way a person actually writes a mobile
       number arrives as the same ten digits: spaces and dashes, a leading zero,
       a pasted +91.

       The country-code strip is the important one. maxlength="10" used to
       truncate a pasted "919876543210" to ten raw characters BEFORE the digits
       were pulled out, leaving 9198765432 - ten digits, starts with 9, passes
       every check, and is the wrong number. A wrong number that validates is
       far worse than one that gets rejected. */
    function tenDigits(raw) {
      var v = String(raw).replace(/\D/g, '').replace(/^0+/, '');
      if (v.length > 10 && v.indexOf('91') === 0) v = v.slice(2);
      return v.slice(0, 10);
    }

    phoneEl.addEventListener('input', function () {
      var before = phoneEl.value;
      var after = tenDigits(before);
      if (after === before) return;
      var caret = phoneEl.selectionStart;
      phoneEl.value = after;
      // Keep the caret where the typist expects it after characters vanish.
      var moved = Math.max(0, caret - (before.length - after.length));
      try { phoneEl.setSelectionRange(moved, moved); } catch (e) {}
    });

    function fieldOf(el) { return el.closest('.su-field'); }

    function setErr(el, message) {
      var wrap = fieldOf(el);
      var slot = wrap.querySelector('[data-su-err]');
      if (message) {
        wrap.classList.add('is-bad');
        el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
        slot.textContent = message;
      } else {
        wrap.classList.remove('is-bad');
        el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
        slot.textContent = '';
      }
      return !message;
    }

    function checkName() {
      var v = nameEl.value.trim();
      return setErr(nameEl, v.length < 2 ? 'Enter your name' : '');
    }
    function checkPhone() {
      var v = tenDigits(phoneEl.value);
      if (v.length < 10) return setErr(phoneEl, 'Enter all 10 digits');
      if (!/^[6-9]/.test(v)) return setErr(phoneEl, 'Indian mobile numbers start with 6, 7, 8 or 9');
      return setErr(phoneEl, '');
    }

    nameEl.addEventListener('blur', checkName);
    phoneEl.addEventListener('blur', checkPhone);

    /* Flat, one level deep, because the far end is a spreadsheet row. The
       attribution snippet already publishes a flat field set; fall back to
       reading its storage directly if the snippet has not booted. */
    function attribution() {
      try {
        if (window.SehatUpAttribution && window.SehatUpAttribution.fields) {
          return window.SehatUpAttribution.fields();
        }
        var f = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('sehatup_attr_first') || 'null') || {};
        var l = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('sehatup_attr_last') || 'null') || f;
        return {
          traffic_source: f.source || 'direct',
          utm_source: f.utm_source || '',
          utm_medium: f.utm_medium || '',
          utm_campaign: f.utm_campaign || '',
          utm_content: f.utm_content || '',
          utm_term: f.utm_term || '',
          landing_page: f.landing_page || '',
          referrer: f.referrer || '',
          gclid: f.gclid || '',
          fbclid: f.fbclid || '',
          first_seen_at: f.at || '',
          last_traffic_source: l.source || '',
          last_utm_campaign: l.utm_campaign || ''
        };
      } catch (e) { return {}; }
    }

    /* One place the transport lives.

       Content-Type is text/plain on purpose. An Apps Script Web App cannot
       answer a CORS preflight, and application/json triggers one. text/plain
       keeps this a simple request, so the POST goes straight through and the
       script still reads the JSON from e.postData.contents. Any other endpoint
       parses the body the same way. */
    function submitLead(payload) {
      var url = root.dataset.endpoint;
      if (!url) {
        // No endpoint set yet. The card still shows its success state so the theme
        // editor is usable, but say so loudly - a silent success would look like
        // working lead capture while every lead is dropped.
        if (window.console) console.warn('[su-lead] no endpoint configured, lead not sent', payload);
        return Promise.resolve({ skipped: true });
      }
      return fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain;charset=utf-8' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        redirect: 'follow'
      }).then(function (r) {
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error('lead endpoint returned ' + r.status);
        return r.json().catch(function () { return {}; });
      }).then(function (data) {
        // Apps Script answers 200 even when it refused the row, so the body,
        // not the status, is what says whether the lead was actually written.
        if (data && data.ok === false) throw new Error(data.error || 'endpoint refused the lead');
        return data;
      });
    }

    function showDone() {
      if (body) body.hidden = true;
      if (done) done.hidden = false;
      if (bar) bar.classList.remove('is-up');
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (sending) return;

      if (hpEl && hpEl.value) { showDone(); return; }

      var ok = checkName();
      ok = checkPhone() && ok;
      if (!ok) {
        var bad = form.querySelector('.is-bad .su-input');
        if (bad) bad.focus();
        return;
      }

      sending = true;
      form.classList.add('is-busy');
      form.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'true');
      btn.disabled = true;
      if (btnLabel) btnLabel.textContent = 'Sending';
      if (live) live.textContent = 'Sending your request';

      var payload = {
        token: root.dataset.token || '',
        name: nameEl.value.trim(),
        phone: '+91' + tenDigits(phoneEl.value),
        topic: topicEl ? topicEl.value : '',
        source: 'blog_article',
        sheet: root.dataset.collection,
        article_handle: handle,
        article_title: root.dataset.articleTitle,
        page_url: location.href,
        page_referrer: document.referrer,
        submitted_at: new Date().toISOString()
      };
      var attr = attribution();
      for (var k in attr) { if (!(k in payload)) payload[k] = attr[k]; }

      submitLead(payload).then(function () {
        try { sessionStorage.setItem(doneKey, '1'); } catch (e2) {}
        if (live) live.textContent = 'Request received. A doctor will call you back.';
        showDone();
      }).catch(function (err) {
        sending = false;
        form.classList.remove('is-busy');
        form.removeAttribute('aria-busy');
        btn.disabled = false;
        if (btnLabel) btnLabel.textContent = 'Try again';
        if (live) live.textContent = 'That did not send. Check your connection and try again.';
        if (window.console) console.warn('[su-lead]', err);
      });
    });
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Article",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "su-post-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Banner" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "banner_fit",
      "label": "Banner",
      "options": [
        { "value": "fit", "label": "Show the whole image" },
        { "value": "fill", "label": "Fill the frame and crop" }
      ],
      "default": "fit",
      "info": "Showing the whole image leaves space at the sides of taller banners. Filling crops them."
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "banner_height", "label": "Banner height", "min": 200, "max": 560, "step": 20, "unit": "px", "default": 320, "info": "The most vertical space the banner may take." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "banner_focus", "label": "Banner focal point", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 0, "info": "Only used when the banner fills the frame. 0 keeps the top, where these banners put their title." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Byline" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The banner image, title, date and read time are read off the post itself. The banner sits at the top of the article card and the title sits under it, so nothing is typed twice."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "byline", "label": "Written by", "default": "SehatUP", "info": "Blank falls back to the post's Shopify author." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "reviewer", "label": "Reviewed by", "info": "Fallback only. Set article.metafields.custom.reviewed_by per post. Blank hides the line." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Consultation card" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_cta", "label": "Show the consultation card", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_status", "label": "Availability line", "default": "Doctors available today", "info": "Sits above the heading with a live dot. The heading and consent line already say the call is free, so say something the reader does not know yet. Blank hides it." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Talk to an Ayurvedic doctor" },
